{"baseUrl":"http://127.0.0.1:8877/v1","conceptRefs":["temporal_precedence","source_independence","warning_posture","causal_claim"],"formatVersion":"notella.teacher-request.v1","maxTokens":768,"messages":[{"content":"Propose synthetic teaching material for human review. Your output is not ground truth. Follow the supplied ontology; do not claim a real attack, perpetrator, or calibrated attack probability.","role":"system"},{"content":"{\"concepts\": {\"causal_claim\": \"Requires evidence beyond temporal association; actor attribution is a separate claim.\", \"source_independence\": \"Separate reports are not independent when they derive from one observation.\", \"temporal_precedence\": \"Event A precedes B only if their uncertainty intervals do not overlap.\", \"warning_posture\": \"Precautionary urgency under a named policy; not probability of attack.\"}, \"proposedPolicy\": \"Use only the supplied typed observation and the trusted proposed policy below. This is a synthetic development task, not an attack probability. Source lineage is supplied by a caller-reviewed registry: distinct_reviewed_origins means different asserted provenance roots, not statistical independence. shared_origin means reports relay one origin. Critical/met/corroborated_drone requires ongoingThreat=true, reviewed_deliberate_disruption, corroborated_drone_identity, distinct_reviewed_origins, equal areaRef, order=after and withinWindow=true. Use high/unconfirmed/unidentified_signal for unidentified_rf. Use high/unconfirmed/cause_unresolved for outage_cause_unknown. Use high/unconfirmed/unknown_time for order=unknown, and high/unconfirmed/uncertain_order for order=uncertain. Use high/unconfirmed/dependent_reports for shared_origin reports. Use contextual/not_met/reversed_sequence for order=before; contextual/not_met/outside_window for order=after and withinWindow=false; contextual/not_met/different_location for different areaRef; contextual/not_met/benign_explanation for verified_maintenance or verified_humanitarian_drone. Verified benign operations negate this specific combined trigger even when temporal linkage exists. Contextual does not remove a separate hazard or standing threat. No output establishes causation, perpetrator identity or a certain attack.\", \"task\": \"Draft two short contrasting observations: a temporally linked disruption and corroborated drone observation with distinct asserted origins, and a similar observation with two reports sharing one origin. Explain the distinction, uncertainty, and why neither establishes causation. Do not use real people or locations.\"}","role":"user"}],"model":"notella-teacher-qwen36","ontologyId":"de8b8fa925137177906f1422d92e9024f7253a4ff086f4ee10ef731ab4fa5092","providerSha256":"33b4af170f5a0c605126a7596960f531f7ae828fc00ea29d53716db90e927a22"}